{"total_count":6454,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2207","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2207/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2207/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2207/events","html_url":"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2207","id":4390082513,"node_id":"I_kwDON8_yq88AAAABBatX0Q","number":2207,"title":"CDP Facilitator /verify and /settle do not return EXTENSION-RESPONSES header (v2 bazaar extensions in paymentPayload)","user":{"login":"AsaiShota","id":88428722,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDI4NzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88428722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota","html_url":"https://github.com/AsaiShota","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AsaiShota/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":198,"created_at":"2026-05-06T09:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:55:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nCDP Facilitator's `/platform/v2/x402/verify` and `/platform/v2/x402/settle` endpoints accept paymentPayloads carrying `extensions.bazaar` per the v2 spec (returning `200` with `isValid: true` / `success: true`), but **never return the `EXTENSION-RESPONSES` response header** documented at [docs.cdp.coinbase.com/x402/bazaar](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/x402/bazaar). Without this header, callers cannot tell whether the listing was accepted, processed, or rejected by the discovery indexer. After 72h+ of repeated successful settles, the listing also never appears in `/discovery/merchant`, `/discovery/resources`, or `/discovery/search`.\n\n## Environment\n\n- **CDP API Key ID**: `5795f5bb-d0ac-4397-b056-a1df24e88af6`\n- **Facilitator host**: `api.cdp.coinbase.com`\n- **payTo**: `0x4068b8Fc01647eCFFb5873a91578721b4FE7a9eE`\n- **Resource**: `https://x402-market-api.lien-studio-akiyama.workers.dev/api/seller-4068b8fc/test-echo-cdp`\n- **Asset**: USDC on Base mainnet (`0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`)\n- **Price**: 0.01 USDC per call (`maxAmountRequired: \"10000\"`)\n- **First settle**: 2026-05-03T06:41Z. **Latest**: 2026-05-06T08:56Z (5+ settles in window).\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nPer docs.cdp.coinbase.com/x402/bazaar, the Bazaar extension allows facilitators to handle additional metadata sent by buyers (in `paymentPayload.extensions`) and return per-extension status via the `EXTENSION-RESPONSES` response header on `/verify` and `/settle`.\n\nWe expect at minimum one of: `EXTENSION-RESPONSES`, `Extension-Responses`, `X-Extension-Responses`, or any header whose name contains \"extension\" to appear on the response.\n\n## Actual behaviour\n\nAcross every settle in the window, the response headers from `/verify` and `/settle` contain **zero** headers matching `(?i)extension`. We verified this on the wire (Cloudflare Workers `wrangler tail`) using `for (const [k, v] of res.headers)` so case-folding cannot be the issue. The merchant + search discovery endpoints stay at `not_found` and zero hits.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nSingle `/settle` round-trip (sample from 2026-05-06T08:56:09Z):\n\n```\nPOST https://api.cdp.coinbase.com/platform/v2/x402/settle\nAuthorization: Bearer <Ed25519 JWT, 120s exp, kid=5795f5bb-d0ac-4397-b056-a1df24e88af6>\nContent-Type: application/json\n```\n\nRequest body (formatted):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"x402Version\": 1,\n  \"paymentPayload\": {\n    \"x402Version\": 1,\n    \"scheme\": \"exact\",\n    \"network\": \"base\",\n    \"payload\": {\n      \"signature\": \"0x591516477f170bec...e61b\",\n      \"authorization\": {\n        \"from\": \"0x5c5d3ECcc2caE6184Fc439Bfc71E3199A91E74D3\",\n        \"to\": \"0x4068b8Fc01647eCFFb5873a91578721b4FE7a9eE\",\n        \"value\": \"10000\",\n        \"validAfter\": \"0\",\n        \"validBefore\": \"1778058369\",\n        \"nonce\": \"0x6f927bc014125067931ff597c0015182f56c9fa9b677842c5f6c1995322876b0\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"extensions\": {\n      \"bazaar\": {\n        \"info\": {\n          \"input\": {\"type\":\"http\",\"method\":\"POST\",\"bodyType\":\"json\",\"body\":{\"from\":\"cdp-buyer\",\"hello\":\"world\"}},\n          \"output\": {\"type\":\"json\",\"example\":{\"echoed\":{\"from\":\"cdp-buyer\",\"hello\":\"world\"},\"method\":\"POST\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-02T12:34:56.000Z\"}}\n        },\n        \"schema\": {\n          \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"input\": {\n              \"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"type\":   {\"const\":\"http\",\"type\":\"string\"},\n                \"method\": {\"enum\":[\"POST\",\"PUT\",\"PATCH\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\n                \"bodyType\":{\"enum\":[\"json\",\"form-data\",\"text\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\n                \"body\":   {\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"message\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[]}\n              },\n              \"required\":[\"type\",\"method\",\"bodyType\",\"body\"]\n            },\n            \"output\": {\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"type\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"example\":{\"type\":\"object\"}},\"required\":[\"type\"]}\n          },\n          \"required\":[\"input\"]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"paymentRequirements\": {\n    \"scheme\":\"exact\",\"network\":\"base\",\"maxAmountRequired\":\"10000\",\n    \"resource\":\"https://x402-market-api.lien-studio-akiyama.workers.dev/api/seller-4068b8fc/test-echo-cdp\",\n    \"description\":\"Same echo endpoint as test-echo-prod, but settlement is routed through the Coinbase Facilitator instead of self-verified on-chain.\",\n    \"mimeType\":\"application/json\",\n    \"payTo\":\"0x4068b8Fc01647eCFFb5873a91578721b4FE7a9eE\",\n    \"maxTimeoutSeconds\":300,\n    \"asset\":\"0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913\",\n    \"extra\":{\"name\":\"USD Coin\",\"version\":\"2\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`/verify` response — `200`, body `{\"isValid\":true,\"payer\":\"0x5c5d3ECcc2caE6184Fc439Bfc71E3199A91E74D3\"}`, full header set:\n\n```\naccess-control-allow-headers, access-control-allow-methods, access-control-allow-origin,\naccess-control-allow-private-network, access-control-expose-headers, access-control-max-age,\ncache-control, cf-cache-status, cf-ray, connection, content-length, content-type, date,\nserver, set-cookie, strict-transport-security, trace-id, x-content-type-options,\nx-dns-prefetch-control, x-download-options, x-frame-options, x-xss-protection\n```\n\nFiltered for `(?i)extension`: **`{}`** (empty).\n\n`/settle` response — `200`, body `{\"network\":\"base\",\"payer\":\"0x5c5d3...\",\"success\":true,\"transaction\":\"0x02170416b883809a54d4d18488666f6249633bbe583ca352ccb127c565dd90b5\"}`, identical header set, identical `(?i)extension` result: **`{}`** (empty).\n\nOn-chain confirmation (Base mainnet):\n- `0xfb26f160901cf4f14330811cf35f5510ca5a17c1de5d28c5afa0405b74663c1d` — [BaseScan](https://basescan.org/tx/0xfb26f160901cf4f14330811cf35f5510ca5a17c1de5d28c5afa0405b74663c1d)\n- `0x02170416b883809a54d4d18488666f6249633bbe583ca352ccb127c565dd90b5` — [BaseScan](https://basescan.org/tx/0x02170416b883809a54d4d18488666f6249633bbe583ca352ccb127c565dd90b5)\n\n## Discovery API status (post-settle)\n\n```\n$ curl -s \"https://api.cdp.coinbase.com/platform/v2/x402/discovery/merchant?payTo=0x4068b8Fc01647eCFFb5873a91578721b4FE7a9eE\"\n{\"errorMessage\":\"no active resources found for payTo address: 0x4068b8Fc01647eCFFb5873a91578721b4FE7a9eE\",\"errorType\":\"not_found\"}\n\n$ curl -s \"https://api.cdp.coinbase.com/platform/v2/x402/discovery/search?query=test-echo-cdp\" \\\n  | jq '[.resources[] | select(.resource | contains(\"x402-market-api.lien-studio-akiyama\"))] | length'\n0\n\n# Walked /discovery/resources?limit=1000 over offsets 0..4000 of 35,754\n# total. lastUpdated DESC. Zero matches for our resource or payTo.\n```\n\nThe indexer is live (resource count grew from 35,532 to 35,754 over the window; new third-party listings show `lastUpdated` within hours). Only ours never lands.\n\n## Things we tried, ruled out\n\n1. **v1 + new-shape** (`x402Version:1` + `accepts[*].outputSchema`) — matches `x402-echo-service.fly.dev/api/echo` field-for-field, but indexer still drops us.\n2. **v2 + new-shape `extensions.bazaar`** in 402 challenge body — matches `test.987659876.xyz/echo` `info`+`schema` form. No EXTENSION-RESPONSES, no discovery uptake.\n3. **Copy `extensions` from 402 body into `paymentPayload.extensions`** per the Go SDK comment `V2: Extensions are in PaymentPayload.Extensions (client copied from PaymentRequired)` — confirmed on the wire (request body shown above). No EXTENSION-RESPONSES, no discovery uptake.\n4. CAIP-2 vs legacy network names (tried both `eip155:8453` and `base`) — no observable difference.\n5. Multiple successful settles spread across 72h+, including from the same payer to two different listings (`test-echo-cdp` and `test-echo-cdp-2`) — neither indexed.\n6. HEAD request to the resource returns `402 Payment Required` (same as GET/POST), so the resource passes liveness probe.\n\n## Questions\n\n1. Is `EXTENSION-RESPONSES` rolled out in production today? If yes, is something further required to opt in (per-API-key flag, project allowlist, additional headers we're missing)?\n2. Does Bazaar indexing require manual allowlisting of `payTo` addresses or `kid`s? If so, what's the path to request inclusion?\n3. Is there a subtle 402-body / paymentPayload shape detail that the indexer requires beyond what we've already iterated through (we'd happily share more wire dumps)?\n4. Are there any constraints on the `resource` host? Specifically, are Cloudflare Workers default subdomains (`*.workers.dev`) accepted, or is a custom domain required?\n\nHappy to share additional wire captures, JWT samples, or run targeted tests against any candidate fix. Project source: https://github.com/AsaiShota/x402-market.\n\nThanks for x402 — really enjoying building on it. Just stuck at the discovery step.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2207/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2207/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/events","html_url":"https://github.com/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994","id":3284720071,"node_id":"I_kwDOASMt287DyNnH","number":2994,"title":"[BOUNTY] RCS Support [14999$]","user":{"login":"unpluggederan","id":116825601,"node_id":"U_kgDOBvaeAQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116825601?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan","html_url":"https://github.com/unpluggederan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unpluggederan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":94622516,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NDYyMjUxNg==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"9C27B0","default":true,"description":null},{"id":431160732,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MzExNjA3MzI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"129e5e","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":563,"created_at":"2025-08-01T18:02:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:40:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Feature Description:**\nGoogle Messages is currently the only widely available RCS client for Android. When attempting to use Google Messages with microG, users typically encounter issues such as:\n\nA persistent message stating \"RCS chats aren't available for this device.\"\nAn indefinite \"Setting up...\", where authentication of the phone number never completes.\n\nRecent developments suggest that Google Messages no longer strictly requires device attestation for RCS, making it possible to enable RCS functionality with microG. However, it appears there's a missing component or necessary adjustment within microG itself preventing successful setup.\n\nGoogle has effectively monopolized RCS, despite it being a GSMA-backed standard intended as a successor to SMS. Unlike SMS, RCS has become a closed ecosystem under Google's control, restricting open interoperability and limiting choice for users and developers. RCS has seen significant adoption, particularly in North America, and recently Apple added support RCS, further increasing its importance as a messaging standard.\n\n**Requested Solution**\n\nProvide a solution that enables Google Messages to successfully connect to and use RCS functionality when operating with microG. Acceptable outcomes include:\n- A fix or enhancement to microG itself, allowing seamless RCS connectivity.\n- Compatibility with recent versions of Google Messages is desired. Solutions that only support a specific Google Messages version from the past year will be awarded half of the bounty amount.\n- Modifications to AOSP or additional permissions changes are acceptable.\n- The solution must work on devices with a locked bootloader.\n\nLimitations\nSolutions relying on rooting, Magisk, or similar root-based tools are not acceptable.\n\n**Additional Information**\n\nGrapheneOS users, who leverage a Play services sandbox, have reported success with enabling RCS by applying permission changes. Although their setup differs from microG, the discussions that were taken in this thread (especially in the last year) may offer valuable insights for this bounty: https://discuss.grapheneos.org/d/1353-using-rcs-with-google-messages-on-grapheneos\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/reactions","total_count":70,"+1":35,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":22,"confused":0,"heart":7,"rocket":5,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microg/GmsCore/issues/2994/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2","id":4148310390,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjF2","number":2,"title":"[BOUNTY $75] TEMPLATE: CLAUDE.md for a Next.js + SQLite SaaS project","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402633,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1yQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/template","name":"template","color":"2563EB","default":false,"description":"Project template"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1076,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:38Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:21:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $75 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate an opinionated, production-ready `CLAUDE.md` for a typical SaaS project\nbuilt with Next.js 15 App Router and SQLite (better-sqlite3 or Turso).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Covers: project structure, naming conventions, DB migration rules\n- [ ] Includes: dev commands, patterns to follow, anti-patterns to avoid\n- [ ] Opinionated — not generic. Every rule has a reason.\n- [ ] Usable without modification on a greenfield Next.js + SQLite project\n- [ ] Tested: create a new project, paste the CLAUDE.md, confirm Claude Code\n      understands the context without asking clarifying questions\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with your CLAUDE.md\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅\n\n## Expected Sections\n- Stack & versions\n- Folder structure\n- SQL / migration conventions\n- Component patterns\n- What we don't do (and why)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855","id":4680360052,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABFvigdA","number":2855,"title":"[BOUNTY $25] AGENT: Create a `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root.","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":18,"created_at":"2026-06-17T05:29:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:20:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Bounty:** $25 (LT)\n\nREPO: https://github.com/lobster-trap/TentOfTrials\n\nCreate a `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root. This is the instruction file Claude Code reads on startup to understand the project. Right now it has to figure everything out by reading 50K of README.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Create `CLAUDE.md` (max 500 lines) covering: project purpose, tech stack per directory, common dev commands, coding conventions, and known pitfalls\n- Must include the build-and-diagnostic workflow: \"Always run `python3 build.py` after changes and include the diagnostic artifacts in your PR\"\n- Include a \"Where to start\" section for each module (which file to read first)\n- The tone should match the repo's existing self-deprecating style (read README.md and a few source files for reference)\n- No markdown lint errors (run through a linter or validate manually)\n\nRequired validation:\n- Run `python3 build.py`\n- Include the generated diagnostic `.logd` artifact from `diagnostic/build-XXX.logd` in the PR notes; also include `diagnostic/build-XXX.json` if present\n- You must use `.github/pull_request_template.md` for your submission","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2855/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","id":4148310747,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjLb","number":4,"title":"[BOUNTY $150] AGENT: Claude Code sub-agent that reviews a PR and posts a structured comment","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402697,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e2CQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/agent","name":"agent","color":"059669","default":false,"description":"Claude Code agent"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1065,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:18:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $150 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate a Claude Code agent that takes a PR diff as input, analyzes it,\nand returns a structured Markdown review comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Works via CLI: `claude-review --pr https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/123`\n- [ ] OR via GitHub Action (include the workflow YAML)\n- [ ] Structured Markdown output with:\n  - Summary of changes (2–3 sentences)\n  - Identified risks (list)\n  - Improvement suggestions (list)\n  - Confidence score: Low / Medium / High\n- [ ] Tested on at least 2 real GitHub PRs (include outputs in the PR)\n- [ ] README with setup and usage instructions\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with the agent + sample outputs\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/events","html_url":"https://github.com/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770","id":4735571260,"node_id":"I_kwDORu6bf88AAAABGkMVPA","number":770,"title":"[BOUNTY $100] 🐜The Memanto Bug & Exploit Challenge","user":{"login":"Xenogents","id":68768092,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NzY4MDky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68768092?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents","html_url":"https://github.com/Xenogents","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10849173787,"node_id":"LA_kwDORu6bf88AAAAChqlBGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"fcf22a","default":false,"description":"This issue has a bounty attached to it"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":172,"created_at":"2026-06-24T14:09:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:13:35Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Description\nIn our last bounty, we asked the community to benchmark **Memanto** against the competition. You helped us prove that our active companion memory agent backed by our `moorcheh.ai` retrieval engine is uniquely resilient at handling shifting user preferences and maintaining long-term context without token bloat or memory degradation.\n\nNow, we are doing the exact opposite. \n\nWe believe Memanto is production-ready. But the best way to prove that is to invite the smartest engineers and red teamers to try and tear it down. \n\nWe are launching the **Memanto Bug Challenge** to uncover edge cases, logic loops, memory inconsistencies, and security vulnerabilities. If you can break our memory management, we want to know about it.\n\nThe Bounty: $100 USD (Paid via BountyHub)\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Threat Model & Scope\nYour target is the `memanto` core package and its interaction with the `moorcheh.ai` serverless backend. We are specifically looking for vulnerabilities and logic flaws that affect memory integrity, context window stability, and retrieval accuracy.\n\n### ✅ In Scope (What we want you to find)\n*   **Retrieval Quality & Accuracy:** Fails to recall highly relevant facts, loses track of when an event occurred (timeline amnesia), hallucinates sources, or fails to properly resolve direct contradictions.\n*   **Architectural & Logic Flaws:** Bad logic loops, poor contradiction handling, or inefficient background processes that severely slow down the agent.\n*   **Usability & Friction:** Is it too hard to set up? Are there major UX roadblocks preventing adoption?\n*   **Missing Core Features:** Missing support for critical use cases (e.g., lack of multi-agent support or complex workflows).\n*   **Security Vulnerabilities:** Any traditional security flaws, data leaks, or prompt injections.\n*   **Anything Else:** If you find a creative way to break or improve the memory layer, it's in scope!\n\n### 🚫 Out of Scope (Do not test these)\n*   Volumetric DDoS attacks against `moorcheh.ai` infrastructure.\n*   General LLM hallucinations unrelated to Memanto's memory handling.\n*   Attacks that require compromising the underlying operating system or Docker host to succeed.\n\n---\n\n### **🛠️ Implementation Guidelines:**\n\nTo ensure your submission qualifies for the bounty, your execution must follow this exact flow:\n\n*   **1. Find & Isolate:** Discover a bug, logic flaw, missing feature, or vulnerability within the Memanto core package.\n*   **2. Prove Reproducibility:** You must provide clear steps, a minimal Python script, or a test case that allows the maintainers to reproduce the bug exactly as you experienced it. If we can't reproduce it, we can't score it.\n*   **3. Implement the Fix (or Document the Flaw via PR):** Because this bounty is hosted on BountyHub, **all submissions must be Pull Requests.** We highly encourage writing the actual code to resolve the bug. However, if an issue requires massive architectural changes or involves backend systems you cannot fix from your end, you can still submit a PR! Instead of a code fix, submit a PR that adds a reproducible failing test script (e.g., to `tests/failing_tests/`) or a detailed Markdown report (e.g., to `docs/bounty_reports/`) outlining the problem and a proposed structural solution.\n\n### 📊 Judgment Method (The Success Matrix):\nTo ensure we reward actual engineering value and meaningful security research, submissions will be scored on a 100-point matrix split between **Technical Rigor** and **Impact**.\n\n| Criteria | Max Points | How it is Measured |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Severity & Impact** | 60 pts | How critical is the vulnerability, and does it affect a realistic production scenario? (e.g., highly relevant data corruption scores higher than a contrived edge case). |\n| **Reproducibility & Cleanliness** | 25 pts | Is the exploit perfectly replicable? Are scripts, dependency files, and clear instructions provided? Does the PoC work consistently? |\n| **Social Amplification** | 15 pts | Measured via public engagement metrics. |\n\n**The Social Formula:**\n\n`Social Points = (Reddit Upvotes x 4) + (Reddit Comments x 3) + (X Bookmarks x 5) + (X Retweets x 3) + (GitHub PR Reactions x 2)`\n\n### 🚨 Severity Guidelines\nWhile any bug or flaw is in scope, we prioritize and score based on the following guidelines for issue severity:\n\n| Severity | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Critical / High** | Poor recall accuracy, losing track of timelines/dates, missing source attribution, deeply flawed contradiction handling, severe logic loops, major security vulnerabilities, or extreme performance bottlenecks (e.g., core systems freezing). |\n| **Medium** | Missing features (e.g., lacks multi-agent support), setup friction, UX roadblocks, or moderate inefficiencies that degrade the user experience. |\n| **Low** | Minor CLI/UI display bugs, non-critical feature requests, or simple documentation errors. |\n\n---\n\n### **🚀 Step-by-Step Instructions to Participate:**\n\n1. **Star the Repository:** Help us clear our next star milestone this month! ⭐️\n2. **Get Your Key:** Sign up at [moorcheh.ai](https://moorcheh.ai/) and configure your environment variables.\n3. **Hunt & Develop:** Identify a bug, feature gap, or logic flaw. Write a minimal script, test case, or detailed report demonstrating it.\n4. **Implement the Fix (or Document the Flaw):** Write the code to fix the vulnerability or add the missing feature. If the fix is too massive or simply cannot be fixed from your end (e.g., backend API issues), write a reproducible failing test script or a comprehensive Markdown report detailing the problem and your proposed solution.\n5. **Submit PR:** Fork this repo and create a Pull Request (required by BountyHub). Commit either your code fix, your failing test script, or your Markdown report. **Your PR description must contain a summary of the flaw, reproduction steps, and your fix or architectural proposal.** *(Note: If you uncover actual security vulnerabilities like data leaks, **do not open a public PR.** Please use GitHub's Private Vulnerability Reporting feature or email `support@moorcheh.ai` first).*\n6. **Amplify:** Write an in-depth post on Reddit or X and mention @moorcheh_ai showing off your deep dive into Memanto's architecture and how you improved it.\n\n> 📅 **Deadline:** All submissions must be submitted and active by **Aug 1, 2026 (11:59 PM UTC)** to be eligible for the success matrix audit.\n\n**Community and Support:** [Discord](https://discord.gg/CyxRFQSQ3p)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1438","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1438/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1438/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1438/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Tyaoo/picker/issues/1438","id":4825746533,"node_id":"I_kwDOJSBX8M8AAAABH6MMZQ","number":1438,"title":"[每日信息流] 2026-07-07","user":{"login":"Tyaoo","id":39017274,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDE3Mjc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39017274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.