9901,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDMyMDM5OTAx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/labels/Game%20compatibility%20-%20Unofficial","name":"Game compatibility - Unofficial","color":"ea6e3c","default":false,"description":"Games not expected to work without issues"},{"id":1041498223,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDQxNDk4MjIz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/labels/Regression","name":"Regression","color":"b60205","default":false,"description":"Confirmed working on an older version of Proton"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":77,"created_at":"2023-10-25T17:54:53Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T23:34:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Compatibility Report\r\n- Name of the game with compatibility issues: Diablo IV\r\n- Steam AppID of the game: 2344520\r\n\r\n## System Information\r\nSteam Deck - latest full 3.4.x release (NOT 3.5.1 preview)\r\n- Proton version: Proton Experimental - set by Valve in Game Properties (as of 10/25/2023)\r\n\r\n## I confirm:\r\n- [X] that I haven't found an existing compatibility report for this game.\r\n- [X] that I have checked whether there are updates for my system available.\r\n\r\n<!-- Please add `PROTON_LOG=1 %command%` to the game's launch options and\r\nattach the generated $HOME/steam-$APPID.log to this issue report as a file.\r\n(Proton logs compress well if needed.)-->\r\n\r\n## Symptoms: <!-- What's the problem? -->\r\nDiablo IV fails to reconnect to Blizzard servers after using the sleep/wake function. I'm not sure if this is a game issue or Proton, but the sleep/wake function on Playstation and Xbox work, so I'm reporting here for awareness. \r\n\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\nLaunch Diablo IV on Steam Deck\r\nConnect to Blizzard Servers, load into game after character select\r\nPut Steam Deck to Sleep\r\nWake Steam Deck back up\r\nYour character is still in the world, with \"Connecting to Diablo IV Servers\" in the upper left corner\r\nGame will fail to connect to Diablo IV servers, returns player to main menu\r\nGame fails to connect to Diablo IV servers in main menu, application exits to desktop\r\n\r\nExpected behavior is for the game to successfully reconnect to Blizzard servers and allow player to resume gameplay. \r\n\r\nNote that in a normal scenario (e.g. on Playstation and Xbox), any server or client related hotfixes or patches will result in showing the player an error and exit the application. This is normal behavior when there is a server & client mismatch. The issue I am describing here is NOT a result of server/client mismatch. This issue is reproducible 100% of the time, even when using the sleep function very briefly (e.g. under 2 minutes). ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/issues/2","id":4582377053,"node_id":"I_kwDOSwQVy88AAAABESGGXQ","number":2,"title":"Polls - (Dev Bounty: $500)","user":{"login":"Kamalaja","id":129144583,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7KXBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129144583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja","html_url":"https://github.com/Kamalaja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kamalaja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11143149096,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSwQVy88AAAACmC72KA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/labels/Desktop","name":"Desktop","color":"d4c5f9","default":false,"description":""},{"id":11143149867,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSwQVy88AAAACmC75Kw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/labels/Mobile","name":"Mobile","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":""},{"id":11143152311,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSwQVy88AAAACmC8Ctw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/labels/Server","name":"Server","color":"e99695","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2026-06-03T17:58:12Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T23:32:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[{"issue_field_id":37415310,"node_id":"IFSSV_kgDOABtywg","data_type":"single_select","issue_field_name":"Priority","value":65470459,"single_select_option":{"id":65470459,"name":"Medium","color":"yellow"}}],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Background\n\nPolls have two purposes:\n1. Quick and easy single selection polls to quickly gather thoughts\n2. Ranked choice polls that help to collect detailed feedback. \n\n\nWe want to be able to support both needs, as detailed below.\n\n# User Stories\n\n## Megan - Group DM Member (simple poll)\n\nMegan is in a group chat with her friends. She wants to be able to quickly ask folks which dress of hers looks best. To do so, she creates a poll. In the poll creation menu, she is able to to upload images and write text next next to them. She is able to set a title and a duration. She also gets to toggle ranked voting and anonymous responses. Finally, she has the option to allow people to select custom responses. \n\nIn this case, she creates a simple poll with no ranked voting and no custom responses. Once Megan hits confirm, a poll appears in the chat. \n\n### Desktop\nOn desktop, Megan's friends see a poll appear with each (smaller) image / text option. The header has the title and Megan's profile picture. \n\nThe results are hidden from them until they hit submit. Clicking on each image brings it up bigger with the text as a caption. Users are able to click left or right arrows or use their arrow keys to go between options. Double clicking on the image selects it as the selected choice. They are able to undo that choice by double clicking again. \n\nOnce something is double clicked, a new button on the poll will appear to show results. Results will be shown in order of most to least voted. Next to each option, a pfp of the voters. If the friend clicks on an option again, the same popup is shown, this time with the pfp of the voters in the bottom corner.\n\nAfter the allotted time, the poll closes. Votes become viewable to all users, and no more votes can be accepted.   \n\n### Mobile\nVery similar experience, except in this case, if images are included, clicking on an option pulls up an image carousal that can be swiped through. Holding down on an selects it as an option. \n\n### Ranked Choice\nRanked choice is similar, except you can select multiple options, It shows you the order selected in both the image carasoul and in the chat. When you view the votes, you get shown the first place selections in order. You can click a button to then see the order changing when 2nd choice votes are added, then 3rd place votes, etc...\n\n## Riley - Moderating Polls (Community)\nRiley moderates the Kubuntu community. An anonymous poll was created that contained negative profanity related to the community. They should be able to determine from audit logs what user created what options. If they have a bot that automatically ingests audit logs, that bot should be able to see that as well.\n\n## Andrew - Moderating Polls (Instance)\nAndrew is an instance moderator. He received a report of a poll containing negative images. In admin, Andrew is able to view all images associated with the poll. He can take all the same actions as he is normally able to within admin on images. Andrew is also able to delete the poll, see who created it, who created custom answers, and **see who voted on it, even if anonymous**. \n\n# Thonks\n- Anonymous means anonymous votes to the **community**, not anonymous written options or polls.\n- Image uploads for polls should follow the same attachment expiries as standard images\n- Image uploads need to follow the same API data logging conventions (associated with a messageID, IP, etc..)\n- Polls should have their own permission\n- There should be a limit to total answers (including custom)\n- Would be nice for ranked choice if the bottom most one is dropped when you go to the next layer deep and it has a cute and fun animation\n- \n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/issues/2/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fluxerapp/fluxer-meta/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93328","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93328/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93328/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93328/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/93328","id":4643737739,"node_id":"I_kwDOEQqHYc8AAAABFMnQiw","number":93328,"title":"[$250] AMEX direct connection - unable to assign a new card","user":{"login":"m-natarajan","id":38435837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NDM1ODM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38435837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan","html_url":"https://github.com/m-natarajan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m-natarajan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":2873246102,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODczMjQ2MTAy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/External","name":"External","color":"a7b8ef","default":false,"description":"Added to denote the issue can be worked on by a contributor"},{"id":2893455829,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODkzNDU1ODI5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Daily","name":"Daily","color":"eb6420","default":false,"description":"KSv2"},{"id":3136662525,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTM2NjYyNTI1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Help%20Wanted","name":"Help Wanted","color":"CFC8F1","default":false,"description":"Apply this label when an issue is open to proposals by contributors"},{"id":3184150925,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTg0MTUwOTI1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Overdue","name":"Overdue","color":"D93F0B","default":false,"description":""},{"id":4664850679,"node_id":"LA_kwDOEQqHYc8AAAABFgv49w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/Bug","name":"Bug","color":"93074F","default":false,"description":"Something is broken. Auto assigns a BugZero manager."}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"youssef-lr","id":9680864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2ODA4NjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9680864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr","html_url":"https://github.com/youssef-lr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/youssef-lr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"ZhenjaHorbach","id":68128028,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MTI4MDI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68128028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach","html_url":"https://github.com/ZhenjaHorbach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":45,"created_at":"2026-06-11T19:52:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:55:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"ZhenjaHorbach","id":68128028,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MTI4MDI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68128028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach","html_url":"https://github.com/ZhenjaHorbach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZhenjaHorbach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"If you haven’t already, check out our [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/Expensify/ReactNativeChat/blob/main/contributingGuides/CONTRIBUTING.md) for onboarding. To join our Slack channel, fill out [this form](https://forms.gle/Q7hnhUJPnQCK7Fe56).\n___\n\n**Version Number:** 9.4.4-3\n**Reproducible in staging?:** Needs Reproduction (Reproduction blocked- Needs Amex credentials)\n**Reproducible in production?:** Needs Reproduction\n**If this was caught during regression testing, add the test name, ID and link from BrowserStack:**\n**Email or phone of affected tester (no customers):**\n**Logs:** https://stackoverflow.com/c/expensify/questions/4856\n**Expensify/Expensify Issue URL:**\n**Issue reported by:** @abbagail\n**Slack conversation** (hyperlinked to channel name): [#Expensify Bugs](https://expensify.slack.com/archives/C049HHMV9SM/p1781198478613109)\n\n## Action Performed:\n\nNewExpensify:\n1. Login into New Expensify\n2. Go to Workspace > [Workspace Name] > Company card\n3. Click \"assign Card.\"\n4. Get a prompt to sign in to AMEX\n5. Sign in and get directed back to Expensify\n\nClassic:\n1. Go to Settings > Domain > {Domain Name] > Company Card > AMEX\n2. Click \"Assign new Card.\"\n3. Follow the pop-up prompt to sign in\n4. Get directed back to Expensify\n\n## Expected Result:\nWhen directed back to Expensify, the connection is refreshed, and the user can assign the new card\n## Actual Result:\nND: When they click the card to assign, they're prompted to log back into AMEX again\nClassic: They're directed back to the domain, but only the \"Assign New Card\" shows for them\n\n## Workaround:\nUnknown\n## Platforms:\nSelect the officially supported platforms where the issue was reproduced:\n- [ ] Android: App\n- [ ] Android: mWeb Chrome\n- [ ] iOS: App\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Safari\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Chrome\n- [x] Windows: Chrome\n- [x] MacOS: Chrome / Safari\n\n## Screenshots/Videos\n\nThe screenshots for the issue are in Slack [thread](https://expensify.slack.com/archives/C049HHMV9SM/p1781198478613109)\n\n[View all open jobs on GitHub](https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Help+Wanted%22)\n\n<details><summary>Upwork Automation - Do Not Edit</summary>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Upwork Job URL: <a href=\"https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022065162815280794278\">https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022065162815280794278</a></li>\n        <li>Upwork Job ID: 2065162815280794278</li>\n        <li>Last Price Increase: 2026-07-02</li>\n    </ul>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Issue Owner</summary>Current Issue Owner: @youssef-lr</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93328/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287/events","html_url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287","id":2878804793,"node_id":"I_kwDOI9Wqc86rlxM5","number":18287,"title":"[Bounty $2500] Bring up microsoft/phi-1 on Wormhole","user":{"login":"thenoahhein","id":60185486,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTg1NDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60185486?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein","html_url":"https://github.com/thenoahhein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thenoahhein/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7931645110,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI9Wqc88AAAAB2MNMtg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null},{"id":7931705964,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI9Wqc88AAAAB2MQ6bA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/labels/bounty_difficulty/hard","name":"bounty_difficulty/hard","color":"C6BB20","default":false,"description":"Hard Bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"Adraca","id":256321285,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0cnBQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256321285?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca","html_url":"https://github.com/Adraca","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":104,"created_at":"2025-02-25T15:39:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:53:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"Adraca","id":256321285,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0cnBQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256321285?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca","html_url":"https://github.com/Adraca","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adraca/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Bounty $500-2500 Bring up microsoft/phi-1 on Wormhole (N150/N300)\n\n## 📝 Background\n\nThis bounty is for enabling and validating the `microsoft/phi-1` language model on Tenstorrent’s Wormhole hardware. Phi-1 is a transformer-based LLM designed with efficiency and compactness for code and text tasks, making it attractive for research, developers, and edge deployments. By running Phi-1 on Tenstorrent hardware, we aim to demonstrate practical inference, benchmark performance, and establish a production-grade implementation for community use.\n\n## 🎯 What Success Looks Like\n\nTo claim this bounty, contributors must complete all three stages below:\n\n### Stage 1 - Bring Up\n\n- The `microsoft/phi-1` model must compile and run end-to-end inference on Wormhole (N150/N300) with no blocking errors.\n- The model produces coherent output for text generation tasks\n- Integrate `phi-1` support into our [model directory](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/models/demos), maintain the same coding style as used in TT repository and measure performance (see [current benchmarks](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/tt_transformers/PERF.md))\n- Include a simple demo script to run inference and show output.\n\n### Stage 2 - Basic Optimizations\n\n- Store temporary results in L1 memory when possible.\n- Fuse activation functions directly after matmul operations.\n- Apply sharding to tensors where applicable.\n- Leverage existing tt-transformers base modules (avoid duplicating code).\n- Document any parameter tuning or known issues.\n\n### Stage 3 - Deeper Optimization\n\n- Adapt model to exploit TT hardware features, e.g.:\n    - Employ SDPA operator for efficient attention computation.\n    - Minimize unnecessary tensor moves by reordering computation steps.\n- Refactor for modularity and internal code reuse, following production standards.\n\n## 🧭 Guidance & Starting Points\n\n- Use the tt-transformers base in `tt-metal/models/tt_transformers` for model implementation; reuse existing modules where possible.\n- Reference the [model bring up guide](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/model_bring_up.md#model-bring-up).\n- Avoid full codebase duplication—implement in a clean, maintainable way.\n\n## 🔎 Possible Approaches\n\n- Start from an existing transformer implementation in tt-transformers (Llama/Qwen) and adapt for Phi-1.\n- Use modular inheritance to minimize code changes.\n- Profile bottlenecks, optimize memory layout, and use TTNN/tt-metal profiling tools.\n- Reach out in issues or discussions for hardware-specific advice.\n\n## 📊 Result Submission Guidelines Notes\n\nBeyond the model implementation itself, contributors must submit the following proof of work. Feel free to open a PR at any stage for feedback, but payout is only made after all 3 stages are completed.\n\n* Functional model implementation\n* Validation logs showing output correctness and accuracy\n* Performance report + perf header for final review\n\nThe performance report generated will be used as a key piece of information for us to decide if the program is reasonably performant. \n\nLinks:\n- [Link to perf sheet](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/tech_reports/ttnn/TTNN-model-bringup.md#41-performance-sheet)\n- [Perf header](https://docs.tenstorrent.com/tt-metal/latest/ttnn/ttnn/profiling_ttnn_operations.html#perf-report-headers)\n\nFor reference our estimated max throughput for phi-1 is 141 tokens/sec/user on Wormhole. A\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources\n\n- [tt-transformers base](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/models/tt_transformers)\n- [Model bring up guide](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/model_bring_up.md#model-bring-up)\n- [Phi-1 original paper](https://phi-1-model.github.io/) (if available)\n- [Reference implementation](https://github.com/microsoft/phi-1)\n- [Performance benchmarks](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/tt_transformers/PERF.md)\n- [Discussion for help](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/discussions)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/84246","repository_url":"htt